---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { getCourses, href } from '../lib/load';
const courses = await getCourses();
---
<Page title="Study planner · Zero to Engineer" heading="Study planner" description="Enter the hours you can study each week and get a week-by-week schedule.">
  <p class="lead">Say how many hours a week you can study. The planner lays the chapters you have not finished onto weeks, in course order, and tells you when you would finish.</p>
  <div class="note">
    <p><strong>The totals here are much too low at the moment.</strong> The chapters are still short first drafts, and the time for each one is worked out from its length and its exercises, not measured on real learners. The projects, which are most of the work, are barely counted. As chapters are deepened the estimates will grow; expect the whole of either course to take many months, not weeks.</p>
    <p>The schedule updates itself as you mark chapters done.</p>
  </div>
  <noscript><p class="note">The planner needs JavaScript switched on.</p></noscript>
  <form id="plannerForm" class="plannerform" data-src={href('/data/site.json')}>
    <p><label for="plCourse">Course</label><br />
      <select id="plCourse">{courses.map((c) => <option value={c.id}>{c.title}</option>)}</select></p>
    <p><label for="plHours">Hours a week</label><br />
      <input type="number" id="plHours" min="0.5" max="80" step="0.5" value="8" inputmode="decimal" aria-describedby="plError" /></p>
    <p><label for="plStart">Start date</label><br />
      <input type="date" id="plStart" /></p>
  </form>
  <p id="plError" class="note" role="alert" hidden></p>
  <p id="plSummary" role="status"></p>
  <p><button class="btn ghost" type="button" id="plIcs" hidden>Download as a calendar file</button></p>
  <div id="plWeeks"></div>
</Page>
<script>
  import '../scripts/planner.ts';
</script>
